  "usage_note": "To say what you want to happen, the verb is usual: *I hope to see you soon*. **Hope of** is followed by an **-ing** form (*no hope of winning*); **hope that** by a clause (*the hope that things will change*).",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "There is no hope to win now.",
      "correct": "There is no hope of winning now.",
      "note": "The noun **hope** takes **of** + **-ing**, not **to** + verb."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "I have a hope to see you again.",
      "correct": "I hope to see you again.",
      "note": "To say what you want to happen, English uses the verb **hope**."
    }
  ],
